  "description": "The table layout adopts a classic box\u2011drawing style. The top edge runs with a horizontal line (\u2500) framed by the corner pieces \u250c on the left and \u2510 on the right, while the joins between column heads use the T\u2011shaped connector \u252c. The bottom edge mirrors this with a horizontal line (\u2500) bounded by \u2514 at the lower left and \u2518 at the lower right, and the bottom joins use the inverted T \u2534. Inside the grid, vertical separators are drawn with \u2502, the intersections of row and column lines use the cross \u253c, and the side joins for each row employ \u251c on the left and \u2524 on the right. Horizontal segments that connect cell contents are also rendered with (\u2500).\n\nThe table is configured for three columns. By default each column aligns its text to the left, adds one space of padding on both the left and right, limits displayed text to 20 characters, reserves a width of 30 characters, and does not wrap words. Specific overrides are defined per column: Column\u202f0 centers its content, pads two spaces on each side, truncates at 15 characters, has a width of 25 characters, and enables word\u2011wrapping. Column\u202f1 aligns text to the right, keeps a single space of padding on each side, truncates at 10 characters, reserves a width of 20 characters, and does not wrap words. Column\u202f2 uses left alignment, applies no extra padding, allows up to 30 characters before truncation, sets a width of 35 characters, and also enables word\u2011wrapping."
